# Build output
/build/
/Builds/
/out/
/dist/
/cmake-build-*/

# CMake-generated files
/CMakeFiles/
/CMakeCache.txt
/cmake_install.cmake
/CTestTestfile.cmake
/compile_commands.json
/Testing/

# Generated JUCE code (legacy Projucer)
/JuceLibraryCode/

# JUCE helper build directories
/juce_build/

# IDE files - Visual Studio
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.ncb
*.sdf
*.opensdf
*.db
*.opendb
*.VC.db

# IDE files - Xcode
xcuserdata/
*.xcworkspace/
DerivedData/

# IDE files - CLion / CMake
.idea/
.cache/

# OS artifacts
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Claude Code AI session settings (personal — contains permission overrides)
.claude/

# AI Context Runner extension — regenerated per-machine, contains local paths
/CLAUDE.md
/AGENTS.md
/.github/copilot-instructions.md

# Vendor frameworks / SDKs under lib/ are source dependencies and stay trackable.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.github/copilot-instructions.md
.cursorrules
.windsurfrules
SESSION_LOG*.md
SESSION_HANDOFF*.md

.codex/
SESSION_*

# Per-repo agent instructions and generated context sidecars. Personal, machine
# specific, or regenerated on demand — none of it belongs in a shared history.
CLAUDE.local.md
AGENTS.local.md
AI_UNDERSTANDING*
.aider*
.gemini/
.serena/
*.agent-notes.md
# .cursorrules above is the legacy single-file form. Current Cursor writes a
# .cursor/ directory (rules/*.mdc), which that pattern does not match.
.cursor/

# Diagnostic captures written by the scripts in tools/. The scripts are worth
# keeping; the audio they produce is not.
tools/*.wav

# The render-regression baseline hash. Local by nature: it depends on which
# plugins are installed on this machine and on a voice recording that must not
# go into a public repo, so the input lives outside the tree and the hash is
# captured per-machine. tools/render-regression.sh writes it.
tools/render-regression.sha256

# Merge, patch and editor leftovers. Git writes *.orig and *.rej itself on a
# failed merge or a rejected patch hunk, so these appear without anyone
# choosing them, and they carry whole copies of conflicting source.
*.orig
*.rej
*.bak
*~

# Secret and key material. None is used today: RELEASING.md records that no
# platform is code signed. That is exactly why this is here in advance, because
# the first time a certificate does arrive is the moment it can be committed by
# accident, and a key pushed to a public repo is burned the instant it lands.
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.key
*.keystore
*.jks
.env
.env.*
